---
source: tests/cli/basics.rs
expression: text(&output.stdout)?
---
fetchloom puts the exact research data a project needs into its data/ folder.

  data.toml, the shopping list: which datasets you want
  data.lock, the receipt: the exact files and their fingerprints
  the cache, the pantry: shared by projects using it
  sync, restocking: fill data/ from the receipt

  fetchloom add iris    pick an iris dataset, put it in data/ and pin it
  fetchloom get iris    just download it, without a project
  fetchloom sync        fill data/ in a project you cloned

a name searches hugging face, kaggle and zenodo. a link works as well:
  fetchloom add https://huggingface.co/datasets/scikit-learn/iris

learn more with `fetchloom help concepts` and `fetchloom <command> --help`

usage: fetchloom [options] <command>

commands:
  add          add a dataset, pin it and download it into the data folder
  remove       remove a dataset and the unchanged files fetchloom placed for it
  sync         place the files pinned in data.lock on this machine
  lock         update data.lock from data.toml without placing any files
  status       list files that are missing, changed locally or extra
  list         list the project's datasets: source, size and folder
  path         print where a dataset or a file in it is, syncing first if needed
  cache        show the cache, free what no project needs, or verify it
  get          fetch something once, without a project
  search       find datasets on hugging face, kaggle and zenodo
  auth         sign in to sources for private and gated data
  completions  print a script that completes fetchloom's commands in a shell
  help         explain the ideas behind fetchloom, or one command

options:
  -q, --quiet         print only the answer, warnings and errors
  -v, --verbose...    say more: -v adds detail and counters, -vv adds debug logs
      --json          print one JSON document on stdout instead of the story
      --offline       use only what is already on this machine
  -y, --yes           approve confirmations, but never choose a dataset for you
      --color <when>  when to use color: auto, the default, always or never
  -C <dir>            run as if fetchloom started in <dir>
  -h, --help          print help
  -V, --version       print the version

docs: https://nikhil-yn-aix.github.io/fetchloom
report a bug: https://github.com/nikhil-yn-aix/fetchloom/issues
